It is very common for cardiac issues to be mistaken for heartburn, and vice versa. Since you are seeing a cardiologist, this is a perfect time to rule out any heart-related causes for your chest discomfort.
* *"Even though my stress test last month was normal, could my recent 'heartburn' symptoms actually be related to my heart, blood pressure, or angina?"*
* *"Are there any other cardiovascular tests we should do to ensure my heart is completely healthy, or does the recent stress test give us the all-clear?"*

### 2. Osteopenia & Omeprazole Management
*Note: Omeprazole is typically prescribed for heartburn/acid reflux, not osteopenia. In fact, long-term use of omeprazole can sometimes decrease calcium absorption and impact bone density.*
* *"I am currently taking omeprazole 20mg daily for my heartburn, but I know I also have osteopenia. Does the omeprazole negatively affect my bone density or my body's ability to absorb my calcium and Vitamin D supplements?"*
* *"Are my current doses of calcium and Vitamin D sufficient to protect my bones while I am on omeprazole?"*
